  "formatVersion": 1,
  "recipe": "Use proof-cases.json baseline and operation grammar. A descriptor recipe applies the named variant, then assigns version. History order is not authoritative; every case must also run with reversed history. diagnostics lists required substrings in the single bounded diagnostic, or is empty for success.",
  "policy": {
    "immutableReuse": "Exact version identity includes build metadata. All matching immutable entries must have exact canonical bytes. Exact reuse succeeds before backfill/prerelease checks, including old majors and prereleases.",
    "newAllocation": "Only stable transitions are supported. Candidate precedence must exceed highest. Compute each required minimum relative to that historical version, using highest plus every entry in candidate.major; take the strictest minimum, not the strictest class repeatedly rebased on highest. A higher major resets the line. No authority or Registry IO is performed here.",
    "prerelease": "GetMinimumVersion(Unchanged) returns its exact input, including prerelease. Other prerelease allocation throws an actionable policy error. ValidateVersion rejects new prerelease candidates and transitions involving a relevant prerelease until an explicit policy is frozen. Earlier-major prereleases below a stable highest are not on the new compatibility line.",
    "digits": "Increment decimal identifier strings without machine-integer limits. Bumps discard metadata and reset lower components. GetMinimumVersion rejects an increment exceeding the descriptor's 256-character version limit; a caller may explicitly select a higher bump. ValidateVersion still accepts a higher fitting stable version above such a mathematical minimum."
  },
